--- commit message
=== dd7086d5aa574285beffc515f9371a438621f25d
KS-1087 (item 1): workflow-approve keeps the pending document when originate refuses the forward

POST /api/workflow-instances/:id/approve used to fire the forward to
originate, delete the pending document straight away and answer 200
"Document has been created" without reading originate's response. A refused
forward (401, measured) lost the document.

routes/verification.ts: the forward is awaited for its status code.
- Non-2xx, or a transport error: 502 ORIGINATE_FORWARD_FAILED ("Approved,
  but the document could not be created in originate; the pending document
  was kept"), and the pending document is NOT deleted.
- 2xx: the pending document is deleted and the route answers as before.

Only the ticket's recommendation item 1. Item 2 (forward a credential
originate accepts) is a design call and is not touched; the ticket stays
open for it. The route is not in the published OpenAPI spec.

New ks1087-workflow-approve-deletes-the-pending-document.test.ts: the READY
cells, plus two assertions the READY's cells named but did not make.
- The 401 cell checks the pending document survives (deleteCount
  unchanged). Its counter was local to beforeAll and never read.
- The control checks exactly one deletion on 201.
Two dead locals are underscore-prefixed (eslint no-unused-vars).

Product hunk and cells authored by the local model (Ornith) from a
Wednesday-written brief; source-read by Wednesday; re-run by seat A.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

